    {
      "_id": "UExLEmgg6vNWYFfR",
      "name": "Fawful's Voice",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/magic/control/hypnosis-mesmerism-swirl.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>A creature the helm is attached to and has charmed hears Fawful's voice in its own head. At the start of each of the host's turns the helm chooses how the host moves and what action it takes (the host can't take bonus actions or reactions the helm doesn't ask for). The host can repeat the DC 13 Wisdom saving throw at the end of each of its turns; on a success it is no longer charmed until the end of its next turn, but the helm stays attached and may try again. A host that takes damage from the helm's side has advantage on its next save.</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
